# Reverse-the-corner (renvers): yellow, right/top/right cushions, then red.
# Source: whitepapers/the_art_of_billiards_play.html ("Renvers": reverse-the-corner or double-the-rail).
# Route reference: http://www.celeris.com/ftp/vp4help.pdf (ball, side rail, end rail, same side rail, ball).
# Goal: a very thin first-ball hit preserves maximum running side spin so the cue returns to the same long rail.
table three_cushion_carom_10ft
game three_cushion
ball cue at (2.800000, 1.800000)
ball yellow at (3.045000, 3.840000)
ball red at (3.380041655, 1.396188500)
cue_strike(default).mass_ratio(1.0).energy_loss(0.08)
simulation(default)
  .preset(three_cushion)
  .max_events(40)
trace(max_events: 40)
shot(cue).heading(14.300000deg).speed(250.000000ips).tip(side: 0.490000R, height: 0.000000R).using(default)
